      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "altText": "Vintage expedition dossier featuring Indiana Jones's silhouette, fedora and whip, with his name, profession, era, and defining quotation.",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# The Man Without a Name\n\n**Name:** Captain Nemo (Latin for \"no one\")\n\n**Born:** Prince Dakkar, son of a rajah of Bundelkhand, India (revealed in *The Mysterious Island*)\n\n**Occupation:** Engineer, naturalist and commander of the *Nautilus*\n\n**Creator:** Jules Verne\n\n**First appearance:** *Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Seas* (1870)\n\n**Motto:** *Mobilis in mobili*, moving through the moving element\n\n---\n\n### Personality\n\nBrilliant, solitary, proud and deeply melancholy.\n\nNemo is a scientist who built a world beneath the waves, and a man who has never forgiven the one he left behind.\n\nHe is courteous to his guests, merciless to his enemies and gentle with the poor and the oppressed."
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "d404e589-fff7-4cad-814a-f96c0e73b3c2"
        },
        "documentOrder": 1
      }
    },
