      "style": {
        "background": "#0f2a38",
        "color": "#e4f0ee",
        "borderColor": "#c9a24b",
        "borderWidth": 2,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 14
      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "altText": "Vintage expedition dossier featuring Indiana Jones's silhouette, fedora and whip, with his name, profession, era, and defining quotation.",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# The Nautilus and Its Kit\n\n### The Nautilus\nA cigar-shaped submarine about seventy metres long, built in secret from parts made across the world and driven entirely by electricity.\n\n### The Ram\nA steel spur on the bow, used to break through ice and to sink warships.\n\n### The Salon\nA pipe organ, a library of twelve thousand volumes and a museum of treasures from the sea floor.\n\n### Diving Suits\nCompressed-air suits with electric lamps, and electric guns for hunting underwater.\n\n### The Black Flag\nA black flag with a golden N, planted at the South Pole.\n\n---\n\n**Field philosophy:** Take everything you need from the sea, and owe nothing to the land."
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "d404e589-fff7-4cad-814a-f96c0e73b3c2"
        },
        "documentOrder": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "8eaa400b-92a7-44a4-922e-001ae1667598",
