          }
        }
      ],
      "style": {
        "background": "#0f2a38",
        "color": "#e4f0ee",
        "borderColor": "#2aa6a0",
        "borderWidth": 2,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 14
      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "altText": "Vintage expedition dossier featuring Indiana Jones's silhouette, fedora and whip, with his name, profession, era, and defining quotation.",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Strengths and Flaws\n\n## Strengths\n\n**Engineering genius:** Conceived and built the Nautilus decades ahead of any navy.\n\n**Self-sufficiency:** Lives entirely on what the ocean gives: food, clothing, even fuel.\n\n**Discipline:** Commands a silent, loyal crew with calm authority.\n\n**Compassion:** Saves a pearl diver from a shark and sends gold to rebels fighting for freedom.\n\n**Curiosity:** Maps the sea floor and studies a world no one else can reach.\n\n---\n\n## Weaknesses\n\n**Vengefulness:** A hatred of tyranny that turns into destruction.\n\n**Secrecy:** Keeps his guests aboard for life so no one can reveal the Nautilus.\n\n**Isolation:** Has chosen the company of the sea over people.\n\n**Grief:** The loss of his family never leaves him.\n\n**Pride:** Believes his own law stands above the world's."
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "d404e589-fff7-4cad-814a-f96c0e73b3c2"
        },
        "documentOrder": 4
      }
    },
