      ],
      "style": {
        "background": "#0f2a38",
        "color": "#e4f0ee",
        "borderColor": "#c9a24b",
        "borderWidth": 2,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 14
      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "altText": "Vintage expedition dossier featuring Indiana Jones's silhouette, fedora and whip, with his name, profession, era, and defining quotation.",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# The Heart of the Character\n\n## What does he want?\n\nFreedom: to live beyond the reach of any government, and to learn everything the sea can teach.\n\n## What does he need?\n\nTo forgive, and to rejoin the human world he rejected before his grief costs him everything.\n\n## His central contradiction\n\nNemo is a humane man who commits acts of violence, and a champion of the oppressed who holds captives.\n\nHe wants to be no one, yet he cannot stop answering to the world he left.\n\n## His heroic flaw\n\nHis grief hardened into a creed, and the cause that cost him his family has become a cage.\n\n## His defining quality\n\n**He is magnificent and unforgivable at once.**\n\nReaders admire his genius and fear his certainty, and Verne never lets either feeling win."
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "d404e589-fff7-4cad-814a-f96c0e73b3c2"
        },
        "documentOrder": 7
      }
    },
